     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hallo,</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">When I install the package in R (function\r\ninstall.packages()), an older version 0.5.0 of hBayesDM is installed (not\r\n0.7.2) and the function I need (ts_par4()) is not found. </p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">When I save the tar.gz File from\r\nCRAN und install it from local it also doesn’t work:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">install.packages(&quot;~/Projekte/hBayesDM_0.7.2.tar.gz&quot;, repos = NULL, type = &quot;source&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\">Installing\r\npackage into ‘C:/Users/AlexNeu/Documents/R/win-library/3.5’<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\">(as ‘lib’\r\nis unspecified)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0in\">* installing *source* package\r\n&#39;hBayesDM&#39; ...<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0in\">** package &#39;hBayesDM&#39;\r\nsuccessfully unpacked and MD5 sums checked<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0in\">** libs<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0in\">Error: package &#39;rstan&#39; 2.17.3\r\nwas found, but &gt;= 2.18.1 is required by &#39;hBayesDM&#39;<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0in\">* removing\r\n&#39;C:/Users/AlexNeu/Documents/R/win-library/3.5/hBayesDM&#39;<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0in\">In R CMD INSTALL<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0in\">Warning in install.packages :<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;word-break:break-all\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0in\">  installation of package\r\n‘C:/Users/ALEXAN~2/DOCUME~1/Projekte/hBayesDM_0.7.2.tar.gz’ had\r\nnon-zero exit status</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">When I try to install the newest version of rstan I get a\r\nsimilar problem.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">At last I tried to save the zip files (hBayesDM, rstan and stanHeaders) and to install them from local. Now I get this error message:</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">&gt; library(hBayesDM)</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Error: package or namespace load failed for ‘hBayesDM’ in rbind(info, getNamespaceInfo(env, &quot;S3methods&quot;)):</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"> number of columns of matrices must match (see arg 2)</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hope someone can help </p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p></div>"
